<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick IV, Duke of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1382–1439</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Frederick of the Empty Pockets</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick IV, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg dynasty</a>, ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> and the Habsburg lands in Further Austria. In 1415 he helped the antipope John XXIII flee the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a>, and King Sigismund outlawed him. The Swiss Confederates, led by Bern, then seized the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aargau">Aargau</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-castle">Habsburg Castle</a>, the dynasty's ancestral seat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-iv-duke-of-austria.jpg" alt="Frederick IV, Duke of Austria" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoni Boys · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_IV_of_Austria.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
